00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.090
anything the franchisor wants,

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:13.160
you have to be empathetic.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.190
This is not a negative.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.683
It's in their best interest.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:17.860
And that's fine.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.308
That's amazing, that's business.

00:11:19.308 --> 00:11:20.141
But you have to A,

00:11:20.141 --> 00:11:22.640
that would be the first
thing I would calibrate.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.540
If you're my brother, I'd be like,

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.540
okay, let's first understand
that they want you to do that

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.060
because they want you to do that.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.610
That has nothing to do with you.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:29.455
You're a commodity.

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:31.650
Even though, it's just the truth.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:32.483
It's okay.

00:11:32.483 --> 00:11:33.853
I think that's not a negative.

00:11:33.853 --> 00:11:35.360
That's number one.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.060
And number two, what are you able to do

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.800
that distinguishes yourself

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:43.580
that still stays within the
lines of the franchisor's rules?

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.360
I don't know enough
about CrossFit's rules.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.200
Every franchisor has different rules

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.201
of how hardcore, how loosy goosy.

00:11:50.201 --> 00:11:51.539
They all run diff--

00:11:51.539 --> 00:11:52.372
- [Male] They're super basic,

00:11:52.372 --> 00:11:53.455
it's use the name,

00:11:53.455 --> 00:11:55.982
have people trained and
so with that structure,

00:11:55.982 --> 00:11:58.560
but I'm also looking
at rebranding obviously

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.120
so that we'd have more flexibility

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.630
and experiences we can create.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.145
- And do they allow that?

00:12:04.145 --> 00:12:05.190
- [Male] 100%.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:08.463
Literally the requirement is use the name,

00:12:08.463 --> 00:12:09.750
we're gonna use the name,

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.475
and it's a marketing agreement.

00:12:11.475 --> 00:12:14.340
- [Female] It's a license, not franchise.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.431
- [Male] It's literally
use the word CrossFit

00:12:16.431 --> 00:12:19.764
and you have to get trained by CrossFit.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:24.180
- I think that if you're talking about,

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.540
there's two separate conversations here.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.010
One, is the location right

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.830
is just a classic supply
and demand conversation.

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:35.028
Is the rent worth the natural foot traffic

00:12:35.028 --> 00:12:37.310
or the way I now think about it

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.050
which is not 1987 anymore

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.230
where you just get the traffic

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.470
because there's a Whole Foods
or a mall or what have you,

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.745
it's how much do I like
the two mile radius

00:12:45.745 --> 00:12:48.650
of Facebook and Instagram ads against it?

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.940
That's how I think about it now.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.230
- [Male] Well I like
that as a good metric.

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:52.340
- I think that's a really,

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:53.310
what I would do,

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:54.930
Tim Ferriss did something super smart

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.670
when he did the Four Hour Workweek.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.640
I mean I heard about it 13 years ago

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.417
and to this day, I still think about it

00:13:00.417 --> 00:13:02.160
'cause I didn't do it and I wish I,

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:03.670
at some level it's so smart.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.290
And I do it with my content.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.820
I'm doing something
incredibly interesting lately

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:07.840
with my content.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:08.950
We call it the machine.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.880
I'm running the same video on Instagram

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.120
with seven different
thumbnails and titles,

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.470
seeing which one overindexes

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:18.990
and then I'm posting it
organically on my page

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.649
and they've done much better.

00:13:20.649 --> 00:13:22.455
I think one thing you could do

00:13:22.455 --> 00:13:27.455
is almost run an ad on
Facebook and Instagram

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:30.820
on a fake gym that doesn't exist

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.290
and say coming soon

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:35.040
and just seeing what people
react to and be like,

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.580
and just getting a sense of,

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.590
I would almost run a fake gym

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.830
with maybe another popular brand,

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:45.740
whether it's Equinox or Barry's, whatever,

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.010
or Orange Theory or whatever

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:52.430
and run it on 15 different mile radiuses,

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.688
or if you have four options of locations

00:13:54.688 --> 00:13:57.417
and just seeing where there's more demand.

00:13:57.417 --> 00:13:58.270
- [Male] I love that.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.240
- I mean for 1,000 bucks,

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:01.884
you can get a read on if
there's more demand than not.

00:14:01.884 --> 00:14:05.913
- So what worked from a
operations side of things?

00:14:05.913 --> 00:14:09.696
When did you get a, did you
get a chief operating officer?

00:14:09.696 --> 00:14:11.456
What kind of worked?

00:14:11.456 --> 00:14:13.580
But also what didn't work

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.242
and kind of the why aspect.

00:14:16.242 --> 00:14:18.000
- That's a great question.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.830
So I always overhire, always

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.286
because I'm anticipating growth

00:14:23.286 --> 00:14:24.763
and that's how you grow.

00:14:26.072 --> 00:14:29.591
- [Male] Overhire as in more
volume as opposed to quality?

00:14:29.591 --> 00:14:31.857
- Well you'd like to think
that you're getting the quality

00:14:31.857 --> 00:14:33.600
but yes, to your point,

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.350
I was like, you seem nice, you're hired.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.514
That was literally how it
went for the first 300 people

00:14:40.514 --> 00:14:43.336
because I was willing to fire.

00:14:43.336 --> 00:14:45.560
And I don't like to fire.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:47.820
I'm kind of like I'll
turn this bad boy around,

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.653
like that kind of DNA.

00:14:48.653 --> 00:14:50.970
So it was a really interesting
double play on my side

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:55.290
which is I talk about hiring
fast and firing faster

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.540
but I also don't love firing

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.360
because I was so into being operational

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.480
and trying to fix in parallel.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:03.647
I think a lot of this comes
down to knowing yourself

00:15:03.647 --> 00:15:04.890
first of all.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.762
So I'll give you a very
good piece of advice.

00:15:06.762 --> 00:15:08.210
I genuinely believe this

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.600
and I've seen this everywhere.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.252
Hiring around you

00:15:11.252 --> 00:15:13.700
on the things that you
don't want to be doing

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.570
is unbelievably powerful.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:17.408
I couldn't be more bullish on it.

00:15:17.408 --> 00:15:18.760
If all of you right now

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.770
just truly take a step back and say,

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.680
what do I do every day that
I don't want to be doing

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:25.800
and hire for that,

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.070
I couldn't be more,

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.010
the reason a COO has never worked for me,

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.464
not my dad, not my
brother, not James Orsini

00:15:31.464 --> 00:15:35.286
is 'cause I'm an operator and I love it

00:15:35.286 --> 00:15:37.200
and I'm willing to
leave money on the table

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.190
'cause I know if I'm a CEO

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.350
I could probably generate more
top of the funnel business

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:42.563
but I love the challenge of operating.

00:15:42.563 --> 00:15:43.645
It's the game.

00:15:43.645 --> 00:15:44.930
I like it.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:45.763
Oh, Rick should be there

00:15:45.763 --> 00:15:46.860
or Susan should take that account

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.810
or we'll create this pro, I love operating

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.230
and I'm good at it.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.470
That's why we're not vulnerable.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.090
When you hunt,

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.446
you gotta be able to farm it.

00:15:55.446 --> 00:15:56.993
And when you know how to operate,

00:15:56.993 --> 00:15:58.590
that's where most entrepreneurs lose.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:15:59.460
They can get the business

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:02.085
but she or he can't operate it.

00:16:02.085 --> 00:16:05.037
So I would highly recommend
hiring around you.

00:16:05.037 --> 00:16:06.637
So if you're thinking about COO,

00:16:07.501 --> 00:16:09.330
are you just so overwhelmed

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.570
or are you trying to be
more physically out there?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.030
But then if you're trying
to be physically out there,

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.380
look, nothing excites me
more for B2B businesses today

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:19.110
than running content ads on LinkedIn

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.080
against the employees

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.368
of the people you know
you're trying to reach.

00:16:22.368 --> 00:16:23.840
Your business is so,

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:28.840
as somebody who's been in
B2C and B2B, B2B's easier.

00:16:29.124 --> 00:16:32.620
When you know who you're
trying to reach, it's easier.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.970
I don't know who the fuck
drinks wine or wears sneakers.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.213
But when you know

00:16:36.213 --> 00:16:38.930
that literally the companies
you're trying to reach,

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:42.530
