- All right, so I have
two kind of questions.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.350
So the first one is

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.334
where I get mixed up a lot is
that we have two audiences.

00:20:16.334 --> 00:20:18.010
So we're selling franchises

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:20.190
to a million dollar network investor

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.730
but then our end user, whose their client,

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:25.260
is a hair stylist making 50,000 a year.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.260
So how to differentiate our company

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.497
to these different audiences

00:20:29.497 --> 00:20:32.110
and then the second piece is we've been--

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:34.097
- I think one thing you can do is the logo

00:20:34.097 --> 00:20:37.370
could focus on the end user addressors

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:38.290
and then the humans,

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.480
whether you or somebody else,

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.120
could focus on the franchisees.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.887
You see where I'm going?

00:20:43.887 --> 00:20:46.330
First of all, you or somebody

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.700
and the logo of the company

